Every strategy needs the same thing: fast, thread-safe access to one state object per key, created on first use.

```text
class PerKeyStore<T>:
    private map: ConcurrentHashMap<String, T>

    method getOrCreate(key: String, factory: () -> T): T:
        // atomic: only one thread runs factory() per key, even under a race
        return map.computeIfAbsent(key, factory)

    method evictIdleKeysOlderThan(seconds: int):
        // periodic sweep so idle keys don't grow memory forever
        for (key, state) in map:
            if state.isIdleFor(seconds):
                map.remove(key)
```
